 ## Overview
-The Voxel Shader Volumetric Ray Marching method is a shading technique for Fire/Smoke simulations and meshes that reads voxel grid data from a Phoenix Simulator or V-Ray Volume Grid [S1]. It solves the problem of shading volumetric data in Maya, where standard Maya materials cannot be applied because volumetrics lack explicit surfaces [S1]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by providing specific rollouts for Fire, Smoke Color, and Smoke Opacity, handling volumetric shading directly via grid data rather than converting to geometry or using generic surface shaders [S1].
+Voxel Shader Volumetric Ray Marching is a shading method for Fire/Smoke simulations and meshes that reads voxel grid data from a Phoenix Simulator or V-Ray Volume Grid [S1]. It handles volumetric shading via specific rollouts (Fire, Smoke Color, Smoke Opacity) because standard Maya materials cannot shade volumetrics [S1]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by providing a dedicated UI-driven pipeline for Phoenix FD and V-Ray Volume Grids, offering specific controls for motion blur, displacement, and emission that are not available in generic voxel shading pipelines [S1].
 
 ## How it works
